# The trade log is append-only: every line is a self-contained, timestamped
# JSON record. When two runs each append a different line, the default merge
# driver sees competing edits to the same region and conflicts -- which is
# exactly what failed run 31032029624.
#
# "union" keeps BOTH sides instead of conflicting. For an append-only log that
# is not a compromise, it is the correct semantics: no record is ever lost, and
# ordering does not matter because each line carries its own timestamp.
logs/*.jsonl merge=union
